{title: Guide Me, O Thou Great Jehovah}
{artist: William Williams / John Hughes}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}
{score: guide-me-o-thou-great-jehovah.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Guide me, O Thou [D]great Je[G]hovah
[G]Pilgrim through this [D]barren [G]land
I am [G]weak, but [C]Thou art [G]mighty
[A7]Hold me with Thy [D]powerful hand
[G]Bread of heaven, [D]Bread of [G]heaven
[G]Feed me till I [D]want no [G]more
[G]Feed me [C]till I [D]want no [G]more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Open now the [D]crystal [G]fountain
[G]Whence the healing [D]stream doth [G]flow
Let the [G]fiery, [C]cloudy [G]pillar
[A7]Lead me all my [D]journey through
[G]Strong Deliverer, [D]strong De[G]liverer
[G]Be Thou still my [D]strength and [G]shield
[G]Be Thou [C]still my [D]strength and [G]shield
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]When I tread the [D]verge of [G]Jordan
[G]Bid my anxious [D]fears sub[G]side
Death of [G]death, and [C]hell's de[G]struction
[A7]Land me safe on [D]Canaan's side
[G]Songs of praises, [D]songs of [G]praises
[G]I will ever [D]give to [G]Thee
[G]I will [C]ever [D]give to [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}
